"2737","idAPIfootball":"722","intLoved":null,"strTeam":"Albacete","strTeamAlternate":"Albacete","strTeamShort":null,"intFormedYear":"1940","strSport":"Soccer","strLeague":"Spanish La Liga 2","idLeague":"4400","strLeague2":"Copa del Rey","idLeague2":"4483","strLeague3":"","idLeague3":null,"strLeague4":"","idLeague4":null,"strLeague5":"","idLeague5":null,"strLeague6":"","idLeague6":null,"strLeague7":"","idLeague7":null,"strDivision":null,"idVenue":"16497","strStadium":"Estadio Carlos Belmonte","strKeywords":"","strRSS":"","strLocation":"Albacete","strWebsite":"www.albacete-bp.es","strFacebook":"","strTwitter":"","strInstagram":"","strDescriptionEN":"Albacete Balompié is a Spanish football team based in Albacete, in the autonomous community of Castile–La Mancha. Founded on 2 August 1940, it currently plays in Primera División RFEF – Group 2, the third tier of Spanish football, holding home matches at Estadio Carlos Belmonte, with a capacity of 17,524.","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":"El Albacete Balompié es un club de fútbol español organizado como sociedad anónima deportiva de la ciudad española de Albacete, en la comunidad autónoma de Castilla-La Mancha, que actualmente juega en Segunda División.1 Fue fundado el 1 de agosto de 1940, fruto de la fusión de los dos clubes más importantes de la ciudad, el \"Albacete Foot-ball Club\" y el \"Club Deportivo Albacete\", de cuya unión surgiría la \"Sociedad Deportiva Albacete Foot-ball Association\", que modificó su denominación por la de Albacete Balompié en 1941.4 El color que identifica al club es el blanco, que aparece en su uniforme titular desde su fundación. Desde 1960 juega como local en el Estadio Carlos Belmonte, de propiedad municipal, y con capacidad para 17 524 espectadores.2\r\n\r\nCuenta en su palmarés con un trofeo de campeón de Segunda División (1990-91), dos trofeos de Segunda División “B” (1989-90 y 2013-14) y ocho de Tercera División.4 Durante su debut en España en la temporada 1991-92 logrará alcanzar la séptima plaza de la clasificación.4 Su equipo filial, el Albacete Balompié \"B\", milita actualmente en el Grupo XVIII de la Tercera División.5\r\n\r\nEl Albacete Balompié es un histórico del fútbol español6 y el único equipo de Castilla-La Mancha que ha militado en Primera División,7 con un total de 7 temporadas en Primera División, 19 en Segunda, 9 en Segunda B y 29 en Tercera División","strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strColour1":"","strColour2":"","strColour3":"","strGender":"Male","strCountry":"Spain","strBadge":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/team\/badge\/17oqja1616436316.png","strLogo":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/team\/logo\/qwbarl1616436315.png","strFanart1":null,"strFanart2":null,"strFanart3":null,"strFanart4":null,"strBanner":null,"strEquipment":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/team\/equipment\/1jhi0q1787136524.png","strYoutube":"","strLocked":"unlocked"},{"idTeam":"153363","idESPN":"0","idAPIfootball":"9859","intLoved":null,"strTeam":"Alberite","strTeamAlternate":"Club Cultural y Deportivo Alberite","strTeamShort":"","intFormedYear":"1967","strSport":"Soccer","strLeague":"_No League Soccer","idLeague":"4834","strLeague2":"","idLeague2":null,"strLeague3":"","idLeague3":null,"strLeague4":"","idLeague4":null,"strLeague5":"","idLeague5":null,"strLeague6":"","idLeague6":null,"strLeague7":"","idLeague7":null,"strDivision":null,"idVenue":"0","strStadium":"","strKeywords":"","strRSS":"","strLocation":"Alberite, La Rioja, Spain","strWebsite":"","strFacebook":"","strTwitter":"","strInstagram":"","strDescriptionEN":"Club Cultural y Deportivo Alberite is a Spanish football team based in Alberite in the autonomous community of La Rioja. Founded in 1967, it play